UID:c5d032d50abecc20@role-tax.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260731T194936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] New Laws Will Lower Costs\, Strengthen Educat
 ion\, and Create Opportunity
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nYou know\, even at a time when Washington\, D.C. seems unable to ge
 t much of anything done\, here in Maine\, we're proving once again that pe
 ople of goodwill can get together and solve problems. Working with people 
 of all parties and with members of the public\, we enacted laws this year 
 that will lower costs\, make it easier to rent or buy a home\, control chi
 ldcare costs\, strengthen education\, and above all\, create more opportun
 ity for Maine people.\nDozens of laws took effect this week\, including th
 e Supplemental Budget. Education\, of course\, as we know\, opens doors of
  opportunity\, so we focused on education. And that's why in 2022\, with t
 he support of the Legislature\, we made community college free for recent 
 high school grads. That free community college program has made a life-cha
 nging difference for thousands of young people in Maine\, and that's why I
  proposed\, and the Legislature approved\, making it permanent in this Sup
 plemental Budget.\nWe also raised teacher pay. We banned cell phones bell-
 to-bell in the public schools. In addition to all those measures\, the bud
 get gives $300 checks back to more than 500\,000 people in Maine to help o
 ffset\, in some small way\, the cost of gas\, goods\, and groceries that a
 re increasing every day because of circumstances we can't control—things
  like the war in Iran and national tariffs.\nThe budget builds on my Admin
 istration's historic investments in housing\, creating more than 400 new a
 ffordable homes for families all across Maine. Other laws extend our affor
 dable housing tax credit and limit rent increases on mobile homes and upda
 te permitting to make housing development easier. These laws also took eff
 ect this week. We can never do enough to create more housing\, but we're d
 oing everything we can.\nThe Supplemental Budget maintains the state's obl
 igation to pay 55 percent of basic local education costs to help hold down
  property taxes\, and it expands property tax relief\nhttp://www.maine.gov
 /governor/mills/news/radio_address/new-laws-will-lower-costs-strengthen-ed
 ucation-and-create-opportunity-2026-07-31
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/new-laws-will-l
 ower-costs-strengthen-education-and-create-opportunity-2026-07-31
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
